# Architecture Diagram

```text
main.py ── detect_devices_early() ──► bridge.start_bridge()
                                             │
                                             ▼
ui_electron/ (Electron)                 bridge/ (Python)
┌────────────────────────────┐          ┌─────────────────────────────┐
│ main.js: window, native IPC│ loopback │ server.py: RPC, SSE, assets  │
│ preload.js: renderer API   │◄────────►│ service.py: state, workers   │
│ renderer/: Preact + htm    │ cookie   │ features/: application RPCs│
└────────────────────────────┘          └───────────────┬─────────────┘
                                                        ▼
                             core/ and interrogators/
                             - Model inference and batch processing
                             - SQLite cache and inquiry history
                             - Image metadata, sidecars and tag review
                             - Model cache and TensorRT precompilation
```

The bridge launches Electron with a per-launch token, which Electron stores
in an HttpOnly cookie. The renderer makes local RPC calls and receives
progress, results and transcript updates through server-sent events.

Batch interrogation checks the SQLite cache by image content and model
configuration. It runs inference for uncached images, stores the results,
and applies tag filters when writing sidecar files. Model precompilation
runs in a background worker, using locally cached ONNX files and the same
TensorRT provider settings as normal inference.
